{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "color-8 3x3 plus masks over a rectilinear color mosaic",
  "transform": "treat color-8 pixels as hidden cells; restore each mask from matching parallel rows or columns and local straight-edge continuation, leaving all visible pixels unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 8-26 rows x 8-22 cols
  mosaic:
    structure: irregular rectilinear patchwork of small axis-aligned rectangles; not a filled rectangular partition
    support: REQUIRED; non-background cells do not fill their overall bounding box, with steps/holes/indentations visible in the silhouette
    local_pieces: small rectangular runs and blocks with varied heights/widths
    local_piece_identity: mask-sensitive length/width evidence is per single-color local rectangle, not from a larger multi-color rectangle
    piece_dimensions: height 1-5, width 1-4
    colors: 3-7 distinct (including background); color 8 never used in mosaic
    background: most frequent color, occupies all 4 corners and grid perimeter
    non_bg_colors: 2-6, fill irregular rectilinear regions made from local pieces
  plus_masks:
    count: 1-6
    shape: exactly 3x3 plus (5 cells at offsets {(0,1),(1,0),(1,1),(1,2),(2,1)})
    color: 8 (azure)
    placement: >=80% straddle at least one partition boundary (cover 2+ underlying colors) [observed]
    non_bg_extent_visibility: REQUIRED; for every non-background component touched by a mask, the unmasked visible cells keep the same bounding-box height and width as the repaired component
    single_color_piece_visibility: REQUIRED; for every single-color local rectangle touched by a mask, the unmasked cells still show that piece's own height and width, and the touched piece is not merged with a same-color 4-neighbor piece
    small_piece_centering: REQUIRED; if a touched single-color rectangle has height or width <=3, the plus center is in the middle cell(s) on that dimension and both opposite end lines have visible color cells
    short_side_visibility: REQUIRED; no fully visible side of length 1-3 may be completely adjacent to the mask's 3-cell bar
    spacing: non-overlapping; min Manhattan distance between centers >= 6
    edge: may touch grid boundary (rare, at most 1 per grid) [observed]
  transform: replace each color-8 cell with the mosaic color underneath; output = input sans masks

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size (H, W) in valid range.
    2. Pick N_colors in [3,7]; assign one as background (not 8), rest as fill colors.
    3. Generate an irregular rectilinear support from local rectangular pieces; reject supports whose non-background cells fill their bounding box.
    4. Color the support into several rectilinear regions while keeping background on the perimeter and in the support's steps/holes.
    5. Use this repaired mosaic as the output.
    6. Choose 1-6 plus mask positions whose centers are within the grid (with 1-cell margin from edges, or occasionally on edge). Ensure non-overlap (Chebyshev distance >= 3 between centers). Prefer placing most centers on or adjacent to (distance <= 1) a region boundary so the plus straddles multiple colors. Reject placements that make any touched non-background component's visible cells lose the component's full repaired bbox height or width. Also reject placements that make a touched single-color local rectangle lose its own visible height/width evidence, touch a same-color 4-neighbor piece, or put a fully visible side of length 1-3 completely adjacent to a mask's 3-cell bar. If a touched single-color local rectangle has height or width <=3, require the plus center to sit in the middle cell(s) of that dimension and leave visible color cells on both opposite end lines.
    7. Stamp color-8 plus shapes onto the output to produce the input.
    8. Validate solvability by running the solver on the generated input; reject if solver fails or disagrees with output.
```
</generation_spec>
